export const postTitle = "AI used. Here\u2019s how.";
export const postBody = "<p>\u201cMade with AI\u201d can mean a spelling suggestion, a generated image, a working draft, or an agent that wrote and tested code. The phrase asks readers to treat those as the same thing. We built AI Used to give creators a more precise way to describe what happened.</p><p>Choose the statements that apply to a particular work. If AI expanded the edge of an illustration, then a person revised and reviewed the affected image, the selection is 27, 94, and 95. It becomes the short link <a href=\"https://aiused.org/1/Y_3\">`aiused.org/1/Y_3`</a>. The linked page spells out all three statements. A QR code can carry the same full URL on a print or physical object.</p><p>The first path segment is the vocabulary version. In <code>/1/Y_3</code>, <code>1</code> means version 1. <code>Y_3</code> is a reversible encoding of the selected category numbers. There is no account or database of combinations. Anyone can decode the code with the published vocabulary and algorithm. Common selections produce very short links; all possible selections fit in at most 17 code characters. A fixed four character code would not be able to represent all combinations of 99 statements.</p><p>We are opening the entire application, vocabulary, and tests for contributions. You can <a href=\"https://github.com/ashrocket/aiused/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\">submit a pull request</a> to improve the interface or propose a disclosure. The short link is also a promise: an existing code will not silently acquire a new meaning. Version 1&#x27;s 99 numbered definitions are frozen. A meaningful edit or new category goes into a new vocabulary version with a new first path segment, while old links continue to say what they said before.</p><p>The link describes selected actions; it does not identify the work or creator. If you need to correct your own disclosure, generate a code from the corrected selection and update the link beside your work. A PR cannot change only one person&#x27;s page because the same selection produces the same code for everyone. Product names, model versions, dates, and supporting evidence can sit next to the link on your own site or in your own publication.</p><p>This is a self-declaration, not an AI detector, certification, or measure of quality. An unselected statement is unclaimed, not necessarily false. The empty code does not mean \u201cno AI.\u201d We want the mark to make a conversation more specific, without pretending it can settle every question about the work.</p><p>Read the <a href=\"https://aiused.org/v1\">vocabulary</a>, try the <a href=\"https://aiused.org/#builder\">disclosure builder</a>, or <a href=\"https://github.com/ashrocket/aiused\">help improve the project</a>.</p>";
